From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 20:24:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(control): deliver ghostty's clipboard writes to Windows
 Terminal

The previous commit made copy_to_clipboard fire, but the runtime's
write_clipboard callback was still the Phase 5 stub that dropped the payload -
so copy would have looked implemented and done nothing. Found by reading the
path back rather than by running it, which is the only reason it did not reach
the user's hands that way.

The callback now walks the MIME-tagged array ghostty sends, picks out
text/plain and text/html, and raises WriteToClipboard - the same event
cascadia's core raises, so TermControl needs no engine-specific handling. An
untagged representation is treated as plain rather than dropped. It arrives on
libghostty's thread and is marshalled, like every other event from that side.

RTF is sent empty rather than substituted: ghostty has no RTF, and putting
HTML in that slot would paste markup as literal tags.

The CopyFormat -> action-name mapping is extracted to GhosttyCopyFormat.h and
pinned by three tests. The one worth having is that HTML maps to `mixed`, not
`html`: asking ghostty for html alone puts only markup on the clipboard, so
the plain-text flavour most paste targets use would vanish.

unitControl 46/46 -> 49/49.
